 "verdict_rule": "BEST(tau) = smallest median among the 9 AI-free methods that give an estimate for every evaluated event (chosen on the evaluated events). A hypothesis wins if the method median < BEST median, one-sided paired Wilcoxon (zero_method='wilcox') p < alpha with >= 10 non-zero pairs, and BEST >= 0.5 km (not FLOOR). H1 (primary): C3 at tau = 2 s, alpha 0.01 -> CONFIRMED / PHYSICS-AT-FLOOR / NOT-CONFIRMED; INCONCLUSIVE if fewer than 30 evaluated events. H2: C4 at tau = 2 s, H3: C3 at tau = 0.5 s, each alpha 0.005 (secondary). Test events: 1.5 <= Mj < 2.0 events absent from the 198-event canon, later than mainshock + 72 h",
 "limits": [
  "Tottori was used in ARGUS development; the test events are fresh only with respect to 18_01 and 21_01",
  "one aftershock sequence; the test events (1.5 <= Mj < 2.0, not in the 198-event canon) were never used by 18_01 or 21_01, but the hypotheses (tau = 2 s, the C4 arm) were chosen after seeing 21_01 on other events of the same sequence; an untouched second sequence is still needed",
  "the M>=1.5 cache was built by 15_01c v3.2 (same picking/QC code as the canon, output name only changed); its dataset-wide amplitude factor differs from the canon, which does not affect cosine similarity or travel times",
  "past-event locations are JMA hypocentres (in operation: automatic slow-layer locations, possibly worse); truth is also JMA",
  "offline PhaseNet picks on full records (possibly better than real-time picks); every method uses the same picks",
  "cache keeps up to 24 stations per event (PhaseNet P first, earliest first); no not-yet-arrived information is used",
  "cache waveforms had the full-window mean removed (includes future samples; removed by the 2 Hz high-pass except for a transient from the window start 3 s before P) and the source h5 is z-score normalised per 30-s window (the scale uses later samples of that window; cosine similarity is scale-invariant except where a window join falls inside the correlation window); the one-sample look-ahead of the cache's central-difference derivative is avoided by not using the last sample",
  "no picking or telemetry latency (tau is ideal elapsed time)",
  "the test events are small (1.5 <= Mj < 2.0); pick quality and station counts can differ from Mj >= 2.0 events",
  "the 2-8 Hz band was chosen after seeing 18_01 on the 198 canon events of the same sequence",
  "the pool now includes 1.5 <= Mj < 2.0 events, so calibration and all medians differ from 21_01 and are not directly comparable",
  "C4's station terms come from past events' JMA hypocentres and truth is also JMA, so part of a C4 gain can be agreement with the JMA frame rather than better early information; C3all/C4all at all picks are reported to show this",
  "C4 corrects only arrived stations held by >= 3 top similar events; each past event's terms are demeaned by its own median P residual over all its stations, while uncorrected stations keep only the static term",
  "H1 (C3 at tau = 2 s) is the primary test; H2 and H3 are secondary at alpha 0.005; everything else is descriptive"
 ],
